00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.749 align:start position:0%
August 2012 passing high over the  Southern Ocean the worldview-2 satellite  captures an image of a bright pink Lake  something very strange is going on here  the image is of middle island off the  coast of southern Australia the bright  pink patch is a 40 acre body of water  called Lake Hillier I've never seen  anything like this a bubblegum pink Lake  the lake looks toxic the pink color  could be a sign of deadly contaminants  or even unknown life-forms  investigators scrutinize the satellite  image could the vivid color just be an  optical illusion when sunlight reflects  off water it can make it appear shades  of peach or gold this can also happen in  satellite images an optical phenomenon  known as Sun glint sun glints occur when  sunlight reflects off the water at the  same angle as a satellite viewing it  when sunlight hits the water the colours  change but this is always pink  examination of other images of the lake  proves the bright pink color is a  genuinely strange phenomenon in every  image it appears pink this is no optical  illusion historical records reveal the  lakes color is not a new phenomenon  this lake has been pink for some time  even early explorers made notes of the  earliest description of the lake dates  back to 1802  when famous British explorer Matthew  Flinders visited the remote island his  journal records the sighting in the  northeastern part was a small lake of a  rose color the lake has been this color  for at least 200 years if it predates  European colonisation it must be a  natural phenomenon of some kind  naturalist consider the possibility  there's something alive in the lake  causing the vivid pink color water  samples reveal Lake Hillier has a very  high salt content similar to the Dead  Sea this makes it deadly for most living  creatures but not all there is another  way that you can get multicolored water  and that is from microorganisms bacteria  and algae can live in some of the most  inhospitable places on earth so a salty  lake is par for the course there is  something alive in the lake the life  form at the center of the mystery is a  single-celled micro alga called Donna  Lella Selena  donal yella Selena produces a red  pigment that is called a carotenoid  these are the same pigments at growing  carrots here the carotenoids are not  Orange  they're actually pink  you
 

